## THE REQUIRED SECTION, THIS ROUND: what is the adapter handed that is NOT the tested shape?
**The property (round 1's, with Tuesday's rulings read into it): whatever a printer, a device answer, a caller, the vault, the token endpoint, the sink or the clock hands this code, it ends in the right typed result or exception, never another exception, never a hang beyond its bound, never a body byte read (nor any member of the body touched) before the credential passes, never a second refresh for one request nor for a request that waited for one, never a value used before its refresh value is stored, never a stored value after `Forget` returned, never an old credential accepted after `Issue` or `Forget` returned, and never a token, refresh value, credential, session access value, card read, password or user detail in a text.** Round 1's H1 to H22 stand with their cells. At least these more; any other shape you meet: give it a cell or name it as a limit in STATUS, never leave it out.
| # | Handed | Cell or named limit |
|---|---|---|
| H23 | **a request that arrives while the first refresh runs** | T12 first start: 1 endpoint call, 2 device calls, both with the one access value |
| H24 | **a new request that arrives while a renewal after a 401 runs** | T12 renewal: 2 endpoint calls in all (1 after the prime), the new request carries the renewed value |
| H25 | **a request that arrives while a refresh hangs (the endpoint honours its token)** | T12 hang: both end `RefreshFailed` at the first `RefreshTimeout` of the test clock, 1 endpoint call, 0 device calls |
| H26 | **a request that waited for a refresh that fails (a first start; a renewal after a 401 shared by two requests)** | T13 x2: each waiter `RefreshFailed`, no endpoint call of its own (1; 2 with the prime) |
| H27 | **`Forget` while a refresh is answering (rotating and not)** | T14: no refresh value in the vault, no access value held, the request `NoRefreshValue`, 0 device calls; the next request `NoRefreshValue` with no endpoint call |
| H28 | **a grant whose caller changes its buffers after construction; an access value empty, with a space, CR LF, 0x7F, 0x80 or NUL** | T15: the device sees the original value, the vault holds the original refresh value; each bad value `ArgumentException`, its message without the value |
| H29 | **`Forget`, and `Issue`, while a check of a fresh instance reads the vault** | A06 forget: a later check of the forgotten credential `false`, the record gone; A06 rotation: old `false`, new `true` |
| H30 | **a device calling in a loop while `Forget` runs, with a slow vault delete and an instant one (1000 iterations each)** | A07: 0 and 0 accepted after `Forget` returned; control (no caller) 1000 of 1000 refused |
| H31 | **a body stream that throws `IOException`, its own `OperationCanceledException`, `ObjectDisposedException`, `TimeoutException` after 20 bytes of a card read** | B06: `BodyFailed`, no body, no refusal fields, the result's text without the exception's text, the read buffer zero, sink 0; the same card read whole afterwards `Answered` (no sequence recorded) |
| H32 | **a handled path under `GET`, `post`, `DELETE`, `PUT`** | B07: `NotHandled`, 0 read calls, sink 0 |
| H33 | **a wrong credential with an operation not handled, and with a wrong content type; a vault failure with an operation not handled** | B08: `Unauthorized`, `Unauthorized`, `Unavailable` |
| H34 | **each refusal before the read (no header, a wrong credential, a credential of another instance, a vault failure, an operation not handled, a wrong content type, a declared length over the bound)** | B09: 0 touches of ANY member of the body (properties, reads, seek, dispose); control: an accepted call touches it |
| H35 | **`StoreRefreshValue` while a refresh runs; a lease sent after `Forget`; a slow vault under the entry's lock; the lookup's timing** | NAMED LIMITS (D30, README) |

